Given that `packaged()` is decorated with `@functools.cache`, if `PACKAGED_DEFAULTS` cannot be read on the first call (returning `{}`), subsequent calls within the same process will return the cached empty dictionary even if the file is later created or made readable, preventing configuration defaults from loading for the remainder of the process lifetime.

